I have completely finished the implementation based on the PDFs and the CSV file!

Here is a summary of what was accomplished:
- **Backend & Database**: I added the `CreditClient` model to Prisma and wrote a script that successfully converted the `BNA_style_1000_clients_fictifs.csv` (which was actually in an Excel format) and seeded all 1,000 clients into your local database. I also wrote logic to simulate the missing `Cashflow` and `Overdraft` variables.
- **Credit Risk Engine**: Created a new endpoint (`/api/credit-risk/analyze`) using a rules-based Policy Engine that computes the exact DTI (Debt-to-Income), scores the client from 0-100, maps it to Risk Levels, and yields the XAI (Explainable AI) Natural Language output requested.
- **Fraud Engine**: Created the `/api/fraude/analyze` endpoint matching the Real-Time Transaction layers (Rules, Frequency, Amount, etc.) producing a Fraud Score and a Decision (ALLOW/VERIFY/HOLD/BLOCK).
- **Frontend Dashboard**: Added a brand new **Risque de Crédit** tab in the sidebar which gives you a sleek dashboard to select any of the 1000 fictitious clients. It interactively hits the backend to display the Risk Score donut chart, aggravating/mitigating factors, and the natural language explanation!

You can find all the details of the integration in the [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/abdou/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/60d63bb5-c1ce-43d4-875c-98208c13e124/walkthrough.md).

To see it in action, you can restart your frontend and backend development servers (`npm run dev:node` in `backend`, and `npm run dev` in `ALGORISKAI`), and navigate to the new "Risque de Crédit" tab! Let me know if you would like to tune any of the threshold parameters!